NULL,NULL,'Think of the minor games you play with your friends in your free time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. Think of the minor games you play with your friends in your free time.\n\n2. After studying this chapter you will underatand the importance of following rules and being polite, in sports as well as in day- to-day life.\n\n3. If not for rules, regulations and ethics, there would be no discipline when engaging in sports and that would lead to conflicts.\n\n4. When engaging in sports, we have to work together with different types of people.\n\n5. Personal advantages of observing rules, regulations and ethics in sports Learning to observe the rules, regulations and ethics in sports will add a number of virtues to your life.\n\n6. Rules, regulations and ethics in sports have been formed for regulating each sport, for the protection of players, to ensure all are treated with equity and to protect the honour and dignity of sports.\n\n7. Let us test our knowledge Place a mark in front of correct statements and a  mark in front of incorrect statements.\n\n8. Mention three difficulties that must be faced when rules, regulations and ethics in sports are not observed?',NULL,NULL,'Understand Let Us Respect Rules, Regulations and Ethics in Sports.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'sports, rules, regulations, ethics, players, game, virtues, able, sporting, well, observing, must',NULL,NULL,'- For example, in \'\'Gas maru kireema\'\' (changing trees) the player who is not able to claim a ‘tree’ has to go to the center; in \'\'Kawda raja\'\' (who is the king) the players lose the game if they step over the boundary; in hopscotch, players are disqualified if they step on a line.\n- This is an example which shows us that there are rules and regulations in sports and we must follow them and engage in sports in an ethical manner.\n- • Observe rules and regulations • The playground should be prepared according to requirements • Standard equipment must be used • Use suitable clothes and shoes • Methods of training should be appropriate to the age • Employ qualified coaches or trainers.\n- When you are able to apply the qualities dedication, interest, obedience and politeness you show in sports such as in your day-to-day activities, you will be able to make your life successful.',NULL,NULL,'- Think of the minor games you play with your friends in your free time.\n- After studying this chapter you will underatand the importance of following rules and being polite, in sports as well as in day- to-day life.\n- If not for rules, regulations and ethics, there would be no discipline when engaging in sports and that would lead to conflicts.\n- When engaging in sports, we have to work together with different types of people.\n- Personal advantages of observing rules, regulations and ethics in sports Learning to observe the rules, regulations and ethics in sports will add a number of virtues to your life.\n- Rules, regulations and ethics in sports have been formed for regulating each sport, for the protection of players, to ensure all are treated with equity and to protect the honour and dignity of sports.',NULL,NULL,6,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(37,1,'English','textbook',9,34,'Let Us Get Used to Healthy Food Habits',NULL,NULL,'We have got basic knowledge about food and the nutrients it contains in the primary classes.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. We have got basic knowledge about food and the nutrients it contains in the primary classes.\n\n2. Food containing oils and sugar Carbohydrates Nutrients Macronutrients Proteins Lipids (oils and fats) Micronutrients Vitamins e.g.\n\n3. Sufficient quantity The quantity of food intake differs from person to person depending on their Body Mass Index (BMI), age, sex, activeness and health condition.\n\n4. Nutrients like vitamins can be destroyed when food gets stale.\n\n5. Packeted and canned food Be alert about the necessary standard, manufacturing date, expiry date and ingredients.\n\n6. • Not having the suitable height for the age is called Stunting.\n\n7. Zinc deficiency Reduction in growth, unable to withstand sicknesses Taking foods rich in zinc such as beans, peanuts, red meat and seafood.\n\n8. What food will prevent blindness caused by vitamin A deficiency?',NULL,NULL,'Understand Let Us Get Used to Healthy Food Habits.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'food, body, nutrients, deficiency, healthy, nutritional, vitamins, different, necessary, growth, diseases, minerals',NULL,NULL,'- This lesson teaches us the need of a healthy meal and points to consider when taking healthy food and also develop our knowledge regarding nutritional problems.\n- Points to consider when choosing healthy food ● Nutritional value ● Variety ● Sufficient quantity ● Natural condition ● Freshness ● Cleanliness ● Food hygiene Figure 7.2\n- By taking five types of vegetables or fruits in a day you can obtain different nutrients such as vitamins and minerals.\n- It is very important to safeguard food from insects such as cockroaches and rats during storage.',NULL,NULL,'- We have got basic knowledge about food and the nutrients it contains in the primary classes.\n- Food containing oils and sugar Carbohydrates Nutrients Macronutrients Proteins Lipids (oils and fats) Micronutrients Vitamins e.g.\n- Sufficient quantity The quantity of food intake differs from person to person depending on their Body Mass Index (BMI), age, sex, activeness and health condition.\n- Nutrients like vitamins can be destroyed when food gets stale.\n- Packeted and canned food Be alert about the necessary standard, manufacturing date, expiry date and ingredients.\n- • Not having the suitable height for the age is called Stunting.',NULL,NULL,7,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(38,1,'English','textbook',9,35,'Let Us Maintain a Healthy Body',