d up to now have shown the things which are important to achieve good health.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. The lessons we studied up to now have shown the things which are important to achieve good health.\n\n2. Raghu : How can we identify a person who has mental fitness?\n\n3. • Since we are not able to perform the usual activities, we are not very happy or satisfied.\n\n4. The following activities are a few that you can carry out in order to improve your physical fitness.\n\n5. • While you are at the marketplace, your mother refuses to buy the toy you asked for.\n\n6. For example, if you are able to understand that your mother refused to buy the toy you wanted because she wanted to spend that money on something more useful than a toy, you will be able to control your emotions.\n\n7. Can you remember that you learnt, what you can do when you have unpleasant emotions, in the first lesson Let us put it into practice There are some small activities that can help us control unwholesome emotions as soon as they are felt by us.\n\n8. Write five activities that can be carried out to improve fitness.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Let Us Improve Fitness for a Balanced Life.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'fitness, emotions, physical, ability, mental, activities, others, teacher, able, good, social, feel',NULL,NULL,'- Physical fitness is the ability of a person to do a physical activity in the proper manner with maximum efficiency.\n- Teacher : Factors such as sports and exercises, rest, sleep, healthy food have an effect on physical fitness.\n- Engaging in aesthetic activities, yoga exercises, meditation, board games such as chess will help to improve our mental fitness.\n- The above example shows us that we are not able to perform well in society when our physical, mental, social and spiritual fitness is poor.',NULL,NULL,'- The lessons we studied up to now have shown the things which are important to achieve good health.\n- Raghu : How can we identify a person who has mental fitness?\n- • Since we are not able to perform the usual activities, we are not very happy or satisfied.\n- The following activities are a few that you can carry out in order to improve your physical fitness.\n- • While you are at the marketplace, your mother refuses to buy the toy you asked for.\n- For example, if you are able to understand that your mother refused to buy the toy you wanted because she wanted to spend that money on something more useful than a toy, you will be able to control your emotions.',NULL,NULL,9,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(40,1,'English','textbook',9,37,'Let Us Be Aware and Face Challenges',NULL,NULL,'We have to face various challenges in our day-to-day life.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. We have to face various challenges in our day-to-day life.\n\n2. Some diseases that can spread from person to person are listed below along with the way it spreads.\n\n3. Diabetes, high blood pressure, cardiac diseases, cancers and mental illness are some of the non-communicable diseases.\n\n4. Immunization Natural immunity of our body prevents diseases and it can be improved by having a balanced diet and engaging in proper exercise.\n\n5. Home accidents can be minimized by watching over small children by adults, keeping sharp tools and pointed objects out of the reach of small children, and storing poisonous substances safely under lock and key.\n\n6. We can protect the lives of all by being thoughtful and acting with care at a time of disaster.\n\n7. Communicable diseases can spread directly from person to person or through a vector such as mosquitoes.\n\n8. Name several life skills, that help us to face expectations.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Let Us Be Aware and Face Challenges.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'diseases, life, prevent, face, challenges, accidents, skills, spread, person, expectations, illnesses, disasters',NULL,NULL,'- Similarly, get the knowledge of handling situations such as accidents, disasters, abuse and expectations.\n- The above mentioned diseases either directly or through vectors (desease transmitters) such as mosquitoes can spread from one person to another.\n- A clean environment will prevent the breeding of vectors of diseases such as flies, mosquitoes, cockroaches and mice.\n- As mentioned above, the risk of illnesses such as diabetes, high blood pressure, cardiac diseases, cancers and mental illnesses will depend on our genes and our lifestyle.',NULL,NULL,'- We have to face various challenges in our day-to-day life.\n- Some diseases that can spread from person to person are listed below along with the way it spreads.\n- Diabetes, high blood pressure, cardiac diseases, cancers and mental illness are some of the non-communicable diseases.\n- Immunization Natural immunity of our body prevents diseases and it can be improved by having a balanced diet and engaging in proper exercise.\n- Home accidents can be minimized by watching over small children by adults, keeping sharp tools and pointed objects out of the reach of small children, and storing poisonous substances safely under lock and key.\n- We can protect the lives of all by being thoughtful and acting with care at a time of disaster.',NULL,NULL,10,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(41,1,'English','textbook',6,38,'Defining History',NULL,NULL,'1 Introduction At the end of this lesson, you will learn what history is, the importance of learning history and how to understand history which covers a long period of time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 1 Introduction At the end of this lesson, you will learn what history is, the importance of learning history and how to understand history which covers a long period of time.\n\n2. (a) My father has told me about the mother of my grandfather.\n\n3. There is a common term used to introduce everything which helps us to study history; that is ‘a source’.\n\n4. For example, one day you may wonder how the scripts that you write today were formed.\n\n5. There are a few methods to measure the time of history in which many events had happened.\n\n6. These two methods are used to calculate historical time on some occasions even today.\n\n7. When the earth is excavated, soil layers under the earth could be seen.\n\n8. The year system based on the birth of Jesus Christ (A.D.) and the year system based on the demise (Maha Parinibbana) of the Lord Buddha (Buddhist Era) are prominent among them.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Defining History.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'history, past, time, methods, years, christ, things, birth, jesus, earth, present, year',NULL,NULL,'- 2 When you learn history, you may have questions such as these; (a) What was the shape of the throne on which our kings had sat?\n- For example, one day you may wonder how the scripts that you write today were formed.\n- Let’s get this clarified through an example; Arahat Mahinda Thero arrived in our country 250 years before the birth of Jesus Christ.',NULL,NULL,'- 1 Introduction At the end of this lesson, you will learn what history is, the importance of learning history and how to understand history which covers a long period of time.\n- (a) My father has told me about the mother of my grandfather.\n- There is a common term used to introduce everything which helps us to study history; that is ‘a source’.\n- For example, one day you may wonder how the scripts that you write today were formed.\n- There are a few methods to measure the time of history in which many events had happened.\n- These two methods are used to calculate historical time on some occasions even today.',NULL,NULL,1,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(42,1,'English','textbook',6,39,'Ancient Man',NULL,NULL,'7 Part I 2.1 The Environment Where Man\'s Origin Took Place Origin of Earth and Life The earth where we live is a planet.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 7 Part I 2.1 The Environment Where Man\'s Origin Took Place Origin of Earth and Life The earth where we live is a planet.\n\n2. 9 Activity 04 Make a collection of pictures of plants, animals and man belonging to different eras, under the instructions of your teacher.\n\n3. Humans were able to do what the other apes could not as the humans had the ability of walking on two feet.\n\n4. We learnt some practices such as building houses and eating cooked meals from the humans who lived in ancient time.\n\n5. The people in that era were able to build their houses using sticks and leaves of trees.\n\n6. The process in which a human being emerged from an ape is known as ‘human evolution’.\n\n7. Their walls were made of clay and roofs were thatched with leaves.\n\n8. This shows how Homo Sapiens, with different facial features, have spread all over the world.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Ancient Man.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'time, years, started, earth, were, people, million, different, first, lived, animals, human',NULL,NULL,'- 9 Activity 04 Make a collection of pictures of plants, animals and man belonging to different eras, under the instructions of your teacher.\n- Man invented many arts and crafts of making various things (technology), exchanging ideas (language), and engaging in aesthetic performances such as dancing and singing (art).\n- Therefore, they discovered a language to express their ideas and arts such as dancing, music and painting to express their feelings one hundred thousand years (100,000) ago.\n- The best example for this is the discovery of fire and learning to use it.',NULL,NULL,'- 7 Part I 2.1 The Environment Where Man\'s Origin Took Place Origin of Earth and Life The earth where we live is a planet.\n- 9 Activity 04 Make a collection of pictures of plants, animals and man belonging to different eras, under the instructions of your teacher.\n- Humans were able to do what the other apes could not as the humans had the ability of walking on two feet.\n- We learnt some practices such as building houses and eating cooked meals from the humans who lived in ancient time.\n- The people in that era were able to build their houses using sticks and leaves of trees.\n- The process in which a human being emerged from an ape is known as ‘human evolution’.',NULL,NULL,2,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(43,1,'English','textbook',6,40,'Ancient Civilizations in the World',NULL,NULL,'21 Introduction Man was in shape of an ape at the beginning, but he developed himself with time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 21 Introduction Man was in shape of an ape at the beginning, but he developed himself with time.\n\n2. A civilization means such kind of cities and the citizens who lived in them.\n\n3. 23 Part II Mesopotamian Civilization Introduction This civilization developed in the river valleys of Euphrates and Tigris.\n\n4. Some vessels belonged to the Mesopotamian Civilization The Mesopotamian people were clever at trade travelling in small ships in rivers.\n\n5. Though it was difficult to write on clay slabs, Mesopotamians did it in a clever way.\n\n6. The well constructed roads in the ancient cities of Indu River Valley civilization can be considered as evidence for their transport.\n\n7. Another important thing that they invented was scripts.\n\n8. (a) Monument (b) Civilization Toy cart made of clay Kunya scripts Pyramids Queen Nefertiti Clay slabs with symbols of animals Golden mask of King Tutankhamun',NULL,NULL,'Understand Ancient Civilizations in the World.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'civilization, lived, were, people, mesopotamian, river, valley, time, cities, indu, scripts, made',NULL,NULL,'- As many important events such as inventing scripts and using money took place during this time, it can be called as the civilization of man.\n- People who lived in Indu River Valley civilization used metals such as copper, bronze, lead and tin.',NULL,NULL,'- 21 Introduction Man was in shape of an ape at the beginning, but he developed himself with time.\n- A civilization means such kind of cities and the citizens who lived in them.\n- 23 Part II Mesopotamian Civilization Introduction This civilization developed in the river valleys of Euphrates and Tigris.\n- Some vessels belonged to the Mesopotamian Civilization The Mesopotamian people were clever at trade travelling in small ships in rivers.\n- Though it was difficult to write on clay slabs, Mesopotamians did it in a clever way.\n- The well constructed roads in the ancient cities of Indu River Valley civilization can be considered as evidence for their transport.',NULL,NULL,3,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(44,1,'English','textbook',6,41,'Settlements in Sri Lanka',NULL,NULL,'31 Settlements in Sri Lanka4 They too had worn jewellery on various occasions as we prefer to wear today.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 31 Settlements in Sri Lanka4 They too had worn jewellery on various occasions as we prefer to wear today.\n\n2. Introduction The first residing of people who arrive in a country is called settlement.\n\n3. The colour had been made of some natural stones called ‘red-ochre’.\n\n4. But during a time between 5,000 – 4,500 years ago, people led a more advanced life style.\n\n5. They learned the art of producing iron during this time.\n\n6. It is a very important historical source (chronicle) which helps us learn the history of our country.\n\n7. In the same way, Anuradhagama, was established by minister Anuradha.\n\n8. Make a list of the materials used to build such a house.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Settlements in Sri Lanka.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'people, country, vijaya, made, prince, stone, lived, tools, been, time, stones, hundred',NULL,NULL,'- They hunted animals such as deer, giant squirrels, tortoises, hares, porcupines, iguanas and snails for their food.',NULL,NULL,'- 31 Settlements in Sri Lanka4 They too had worn jewellery on various occasions as we prefer to wear today.\n- Introduction The first residing of people who arrive in a country is called settlement.\n- The colour had been made of some natural stones called ‘red-ochre’.\n- But during a time between 5,000 – 4,500 years ago, people led a more advanced life style.\n- They learned the art of producing iron during this time.\n- It is a very important historical source (chronicle) which helps us learn the history of our country.',NULL,NULL,4,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(45,1,'English','textbook',6,42,'Our Brave Kings',NULL,NULL,'37 Introduction The ruler needs to be virtuous and intelligent to develop any country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 37 Introduction The ruler needs to be virtuous and intelligent to develop any country.\n\n2. On their return to Sri Lanka, emperor Ashoka sent what was necessary for king Tissa for his coronation.\n\n3. The king did so with the intention of constructing more Buddhist temples and making the city more beautiful.\n\n4. The tusker called ‘Kandula’ too was a great support to the king.\n\n5. There was a terrible famine during the time when King Valagamba was hiding in the forest.\n\n6. He placed the same quantity of jasmine flowers among the other varieties too.\n\n7. It is believed that the ‘Pati’ (belt) relic of the Lord Buddha has been deposited in the ‘Jethawana Dageba’ built by him.\n\n8. Name the irrigation works constructed by King Dhathusena.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Our Brave Kings.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'king, country, constructed, anuradhapura, city, great, dutugemunu, devanampiyatissa, stupa, maha, named, built',NULL,NULL,'- The sailors, who travelled in ships in the Indian Ocean, knew our small island by various names such as Sihaladeepa, Silediba, Ceylan, Serendib and Taprobane.\n- You should be determined to be a respectable citizen by taking the king Pandukabhaya\'s life as an example.\n- In addition, he constructed places such as ponds for the use of the Bhikkhus.\n- The way that king Valagamba strived to work for the benefit of the country by overcoming the hardships he encountered sets a good example to you.',NULL,NULL,'- 37 Introduction The ruler needs to be virtuous and intelligent to develop any country.\n- On their return to Sri Lanka, emperor Ashoka sent what was necessary for king Tissa for his coronation.\n- The king did so with the intention of constructing more Buddhist temples and making the city more beautiful.\n- The tusker called ‘Kandula’ too was a great support to the king.\n- There was a terrible famine during the time when King Valagamba was hiding in the forest.\n- He placed the same quantity of jasmine flowers among the other varieties too.',NULL,NULL,5,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:10','2026-08-06 17:15:10'),(46,1,'English','textbook',8,43,'Algorithm and Flow Charts',NULL,NULL,'55 Algorithm and Flow Charts5Process of Solving Practical Problems5.1Imagine that a group of relatives have arrived when you were alone in the house.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 55 Algorithm and Flow Charts5Process of Solving Practical Problems5.1Imagine that a group of relatives have arrived when you were alone in the house.\n\n2. Problem Solving5.1.1The problem needs to be analyzed well before solving it.\n\n3. All the fruits mixed with sugar should be washed again.\n\n4. While beating, add sugar little by littleStep 06Add the eggs one by one to the sugar and butter mixture Step 07Add the dissolved chocolateStep 08Add milkStep 09Put the mixture into the baking tray and bake itStep 10Let it cool after bakingStep 11Decorate as you wish and serve itStep 12End\n\n5. 60 Used to show an action/a processEg: 