and respect towards you among your relatives.\n\n8. Benefits achieved by following these traditions Traditions followed by your family 1 2 3 4 5  State several measures in your exercise book that can be taken to develop the cooperation and cordiality among the people living in your area.',NULL,NULL,'Understand Our Family.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'family, life, various, society, members, good, mother, activities, parents, shyama, qualities, person',NULL,NULL,'- Common features that can be seen in a family When we consider the composition, performance and the existence of a family, we can observe several significant features of a family unit.\n- Column IIColumn I The procedure to be followed in order to achieve the objectives Objectives Joining as a prefect of the school prefect board Joining the school band Joining the school debate team Activity 1.2\n- ▪ Achieving a national level victory in any field of aesthetic of your choice Activity 1.3 Self esteem Read the story given below Little Shyama’s Donation Shyama is a student studying in Grade 5.\n- Good Media Programmes You have the opportunity of using printed media such as newspapers, magazines and electronic media such as television, radio, internet during your leisure.',NULL,NULL,'- The society that we live in is a collection of a number of family units.\n- State the procedures that you should follow to fulfill the objectives in column II.\n- It is quite important to choose things which are proper and suitable to establish your identity and dignity.\n- Diverse occasions and experiences of life, and the splendour of nature can be expressed through various creations.\n- ● Engage in religious activities ● Walk ● Recite poems and singing ● Aesthetic activities like drawing ● Read books ● Admire the beauty of the surroundings ● Listen to the radio\n- It is quite essential to engage in a legitimate occupation to earn a sufficient income for the survival and progress of the family.',NULL,NULL,1,'active','2026-08-06 17:15:12','2026-08-06 17:15:12'),(262,2,'English','textbook',19,135,'Our Society',NULL,NULL,'For example, people of hunting era had spent a collective life and worked in cooperation to fulfill their food requirements and their basic needs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. For example, people of hunting era had spent a collective life and worked in cooperation to fulfill their food requirements and their basic needs.\n\n2. Thus, if we maintain cordial relationships with neighbours we can keep friendly human ties.\n\n3.  Make a list of sources in your school, to obtain the data and information easily.\n\n4. It is our duty to improve the psycho-social skills to face such situations successfully.\n\n5. Qualities to be improved to live as a good citizen in society Man is a great treasure.\n\n6. Once they lose the usual duty – bounded environment, in which they worked for a long period of time, they are liable to face physical and mental inconveniences.\n\n7. Steps to win challenges ² Building up life objectives or targets ² Adapt to an affordable life style ² Taking correct decisions\n\n8.  What are your responsibilities with regard to your school?',NULL,NULL,'Understand Our Society.\nExplain its main ideas.\nUse the lesson knowledge in revision activities.',NULL,NULL,'society, children, rights, people, good, relationships, face, information, institutions, challenges, life, human',NULL,NULL,'- For example, people of hunting era had spent a collective life and worked in cooperation to fulfill their food requirements and their basic needs.\n- There, the parents maintain relationships with their children by fulfilling their obligations such as feeding, safeguarding, providing education, helping to satisfy other needs, protecting from diseases and settling them in marriage.\n- We should maintain some good human qualities such as being peaceful, brotherhood, cooperation, helping others, giving refuge and