ook',25,239,'Multicultural Society',NULL,NULL,'51 03 Multicultural Society Introduction People belonging to different races, and different religions and people who speak different languages may live in one country.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 51 03 Multicultural Society Introduction People belonging to different races, and different religions and people who speak different languages may live in one country.\n\n2. Buddhists, Christians, Hindus, Islam as well as those who speak Sinhala, Tamil and English also live in this country.\n\n3. 57 Existence of different customs and traditions Different customs and traditions can be seen in a multicultural society.\n\n4. There are many cultural places related to those cultures.\n\n5. In addition to that, on every fullmoon poya day, sil and meditation programmes and other meritorious activities are organized.\n\n6. Get the guidance and instructions of your subject teacher for this.\n\n7. To own a glorious culture, one should safeguard one\'s own cultural identity.\n\n8. It is a reliable way to build up national unity and peace among various ethnic, racial and religious groups.',NULL,NULL,'Understand the main ideas in Multicultural Society and use them in revision.',NULL,NULL,'culture, different, multicultural, society, cultural, religious, country, customs, groups, live, ethnic, festival',NULL,NULL,'- They observe different religions, speak different languages and follow different customs and rituals.\n- Most of the countries such as United States of America, and India are countries with multicultural societies.\n- Some of the examples for countries with multicultural societies are as follows: Sri Lanka India The United States of America The Great Britain Activity ² Construct a simple definition on culture, through the facts you learn about culture.\n- In such a society, all those who speak different languages, observe different religions and follow different customs should work together.',NULL,NULL,'- 51 03 Multicultural Society Introduction People belonging to different races, and different religions and people who speak different languages may live in one country.\n- Buddhists, Christians, Hindus, Islam as well as those who speak Sinhala, Tamil and English also live in this country.\n- 57 Existence of different customs and traditions Different customs and traditions can be seen in a multicultural society.\n- There are many cultural places related to those cultures.\n- In addition to that, on every fullmoon poya day, sil and meditation programmes and other meritorious activities are organized.\n- Get the guidance and instructions of your subject teacher for this.',NULL,NULL,3,'inactive','2026-08-06 17:31:15','2026-08-10 09:13:24'),(376,3,'English','textbook',25,240,'Contemporary Issues',NULL,NULL,'69 04 Contemporary Issues Introduction Natural disasters, accidents, hazards, improper life habits can be cited as the most powerful challenges for the protective existence of human society.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 69 04 Contemporary Issues Introduction Natural disasters, accidents, hazards, improper life habits can be cited as the most powerful challenges for the protective existence of human society.\n\n2. Houses, tourist hotels, fishing harbours and boats, vehicles and other properties were heavily damaged.\n\n3. Since accidents and disasters around us are likely to happen at any time, we must be vigilant, aware and act diligently.\n\n4. e.g.- ² Driving after liquor ² Driving under the effect of bad impulses and emotions (anger, sadness, depression, extreme happiness) ² Using mobile phones while driving ² Smoking and use of narcotics The numbers of accidents taking place due to these reasons keep increasing day by day.\n\n5. Condition of vehicles Road accidents have also increased due to poor conditions of vehicles.\n\n6. Affordable lifestyles and sustainable development With development, the modern world faces many differences.\n\n7. Disposal of garbage improperly Disposal of garbage properly Always dispose of your garbage in the correct containers.\n\n8.  It is the duty of all responsible people to actively help victims in the event of a disaster.',NULL,NULL,'Understand the main ideas in Contemporary Issues and use them in revision.',NULL,NULL,'accidents, disasters, road, natural, caused, avoid, disaster, development, water, take, food, human',NULL,NULL,'- Flooding is natural, but human activity contributes mostly towards flooding.\n- It directly affected the coastal areas of Sri Lanka and other countries such as India, Indonesia and Thailand.\n- 78 Activity ² Prepare a file of information which consists of newspaper reports, photographs etc.\n- We also use different types of fireworks in our homes on festive occasions such as Sinhala - Hindu New Year and Christmas.',NULL,NULL,'- 69 04 Contemporary Issues Introduction Natural disasters, accidents, hazards, improper life habits can be cited as the most powerful challenges for the protective existence of human society.\n- Houses, tourist hotels, fishing harbours and boats, vehicles and other properties were heavily damaged.\n- Since accidents and disasters around us are likely to happen at any time, we must be vigilant, aware and act diligently.\n- e.g.- ² Driving after liquor ² Driving under the effect of bad impulses and emotions (anger, sadness, depression, extreme happiness) ² Using mobile phones while driving ² Smoking and use of narcotics The numbers of accidents taking place due to these reasons keep increasing day by day.\n- Condition of vehicles Road accidents have also increased due to poor conditions of vehicles.\n- Affordable lifestyles and sustainable development With development, the modern world faces many differences.',NULL,NULL,4,'inactive','2026-08-06 17:31:15','2026-08-10 09:13:24'),(377,3,'English','textbook',25,241,'Let\'s Overcome Challenges by Solving Problems',NULL,NULL,'104 05 Let’s Overcome Challenges by Solving Problems Introduction A person has to face various challenges and problems in his personal life as well as in social life.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. 104 05 Let’s Overcome Challenges by Solving Problems Introduction A person has to face various challenges and problems in his personal life as well as in social life.\n\n2. Though we get temporary solutions through this, it is not a correct solution to the problem.\n\n3. When finding solutions to a problem, it is of utmost importance to have a good understanding and a realization of it.\n\n4. So, with the determination of empowering his family and looking after his parents, he attended school daily on clutches walking around six miles, carrying his school bag.\n\n5. By improving these qualities, your personality too can be enhanced.\n\n6. When you work without a goal or target, it becomes unsuccessful as it possesses no strong foundation.\n\n7. Participating in Olympic Games then, might have been only a dream to her as she was born and educated amidst-economic difficulties in a difficult area in Sri Lanka.\n\n8. Problem/ Challenge Creation invented Louis Braille lost his eye sight at the age of 15 by an accident Braille system of reading and writing Activity  Associating information and reports in newspapers, discuss the ways of freeing school children who are subjected to various problems and challenges.',NULL,NULL,'Understand the main ideas in Let\'s Overcome Challenges by Solving Problems and use them in revision.',NULL,NULL,'challenges, problem, problems, solutions, various, challenge, life, important, overcome, face, well, successfully',NULL,NULL,'- For an example, though crossing a river is a problem to a rabbit, it is not a problem to a tortoise.\n- 105 A problem can be defined as a barrier or an obstacle that blocks reaching a certain activity, condition or situation.\n- For example, the steps that could be used to solve the problem of being weak in your subject achievement can be presented as follows;\n- 112 Activit