icles The main reason for such changes in physical and chemical properties is the increase in the surface area (A) to volume (V) ratio (A/V) when the particles size decreases.\n\n4. It also shows unexpected electronic and electrical properties.\n\n5. One way of doing this is the introduction of nano particles which are similar to HDL, a type of favourable cholesterol, to remove lipid deposits in blood vessels.\n\n6. ² Household items like high quality detergents and bleaching agents, air filters, water filters, antiseptics, stain and dirt resistant paints can be manufactured using nanotechnology.\n\n7. ² The best natural nanosystem is the cell, which is the structural and functional unit of organisms.\n\n8. Technical Terms Nanometer - kefkdaógrh - |÷Úõ «ØÓº Nanotechnology - kefkda ;dlaIKh - |÷Úõ öuõÈÀ~m£® Nanoparticle - kefkda wxY= - |÷Úõ xoUøPPÒ Lotus effect - f,dagia wdprKh - ÷»õmhì ÂøÍÄ Activated carbon - il%Sh ldnka - öuõÈØ£k® Põ£ß Fullerene - *q,Íka - ¦ÍŸß Graphene - .%e*Ska - Qµ¥ß',NULL,NULL,'Understand the main ideas in Nanotechnology and Its Applications and use them in revision.',NULL,NULL,'nanotechnology, science, applications, carbon, surface, nanoscale, lotus, area, like, nano, water, particles',NULL,NULL,'- Science | Nanotechnology and its Applications 103Science | Nanotechnology and its ApplicationsPB Observe well, the figure 16.1 given below.\n- Let us do the activity 16.1 to get an idea of such things and their functioning.\n- Science | Nanotechnology and its Applications 107Science | Nanotechnology and its Applications106 Activity 16.1 You will need :- Untorn lotus or alocasia leaf Method :- ² Put few drops of water on the leaf and observe.\n- Lotus effect The self cleansing activity of lotus leaves because of the hydrophobic condition on its surface is known as lotus effect.',NULL,NULL,'- Science | Nanotechnology and its Applications 103Science | Nanotechnology and its ApplicationsPB Observe well, the figure 16.1 given below.\n- Nanotechnology could not really took off until the electron microscopy became popular.\n- Surface area of nano particles The main reason for such changes in physical and chemical properties is the increase in the surface area (A) to volume (V) ratio (A/V) when the particles size decreases.\n- It also shows unexpected electronic and electrical properties.\n- One way of doing this is the introduction of nano particles which are similar to HDL, a type of favourable cholesterol, to remove lipid deposits in blood vessels.\n- ² Household items like high quality detergents and bleaching agents, air filters, water filters, antiseptics, stain and dirt resistant paints can be manufactured using nanotechnology.',NULL,NULL,16,'inactive','2026-08-06 17:31:18','2026-08-10 09:13:27'),(509,4,'English','textbook',35,373,'Lightning Accidents',NULL,NULL,'Science | Lightning Accidents 119Science | Lightning AccidentsPB Recall what you have learnt about the accidents caused by lightning in grade 7.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. Science | Lightning Accidents 119Science | Lightning AccidentsPB Recall what you have learnt about the accidents caused by lightning in grade 7.\n\n2. According to the above newspaper reports (figure 17.1), it has been observed that the lightning activity is at its peak in the months of March-April and October-November.\n\n3. When, very large amounts of charges are developed like this, a moment will arise where electricity can flow even through air.\n\n4. The reason for this is that the speed of light is very high whereas the speed of sound is much less than the speed of light.\n\n5. Accordingly, you may understand that the thunder accompanying is also intense.\n\n6. Therefore, measures should be taken to minimize the losses caused by lightning.\n\n7. ² In a lightning bolt, flow of a high current occurs instantaneously due to the high potential difference created between the clouds and the Earth.\n\n8. Air with water vapour moving up gets cooled to form clouds.',NULL,NULL,'Understand the main ideas in Lightning Accidents and use them in revision.',NULL,NULL,'lightning, accidents, cloud, charges, science, sound, light, current, clouds, ground, tree, caused',NULL,NULL,'- Note down the months in which the lightning activity is highest.\n- According to the above newspaper reports (figure 17.1), it has been observed that the lightning activity is at its peak in the months of March-April and October-November.\n- Assignment 17.2 Observe continuously the changes taking place in a cumulonimbus cloud formed in the afternoon during the inter-monsoonal period and Observe the following.\n- Let us do the activity 17.2 to produce an electric spark (a teacher demonstration).',NULL,NULL,'- Science | Lightning Accidents 119Science | Lightning AccidentsPB Recall what you have learnt about the accidents caused by lightning in grade 7.\n- According to the above newspaper reports (figure 17.1), it has been observed that the lightning activity is at its peak in the months of March-April and October-November.\n- When, very large amounts of charges are developed like this, a moment will arise where electricity can flow even through air.\n- The reason for this is that the speed of light is very high whereas the speed of sound is much less than the speed of light.\n- Accordingly, you may understand that the thunder accompanying is also intense.\n- Therefore, measures should be taken to minimize the losses caused by lightning.',NULL,NULL,17,'inactive','2026-08-06 17:31:18','2026-08-10 09:13:27'),(510,4,'English','textbook',35,374,'Natural Disasters',NULL,NULL,'Science | Natural DisastersPB Science | Natural Disasters 129 The losses brought about on humans, animals and property by a natural process without the interference of man is named a natural disaster.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SHORT NOTES\n\n1. Science | Natural DisastersPB Science | Natural Disasters 129 The losses brought about on humans, animals and property by a natural process without the inte